From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Sep 2026 14:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Set training logging up before the config is read

0020-Remove-tf.compat.v1-from-the-pose-engine.patch put load_config() ahead of
setup_logging() in core/train.py's train(), and a single-animal TensorFlow
training has printed no progress and written no log.txt since:
config.cfg_from_file() calls logging.info(), which runs logging.basicConfig()
implicitly and installs a stderr handler on the root logger at level WARNING.
The setup_logging() that follows calls basicConfig(filename="log.txt",
level=INFO), and basicConfig does nothing at all once the root logger has a
handler, so the file handler is never installed and the root level stays at
WARNING.

On the bundled openfield project, 40 iterations, resnet_50:

                          stdout "iteration:" lines   log.txt
    DeepLabCut 3.0.1                              8   2668 bytes
    patches 0001-0024                             0   absent
    with this patch                               8   2668 bytes

learning_stats.csv was still written, so the loss was recoverable, but
someone watching a multi-day run saw nothing and lost the training log.
Multi-animal training was unaffected: it still called setup_logging() first.

train() now chdirs and sets logging up before it reads the config, which is
the order DeepLabCut 3.0.1 used, and passes the config it loaded on to
legacy_tf1.train() instead of having it read the same file a second time.
